# Proof run 5 — Single-page modern dashboard (UI upgrade)

- **Date:** 2026-11-15
- **Machine:** this Linux VM (Temurin 24.0.2); target = bundled LoadApp
  (G1, -Xmx256m), PID 4696 — the same proof discipline as runs 1–4.
- **Code:** appraan working tree on top of 747698f (UI upgrade:
  Pages.java rework, UiServer `/` passes the current snapshot,
  RenderProof dashboard assertions).
- **Artefacts:** everything in `proof/run5/` (fetched pages + API
  payloads + the kernel fixture copy).

## What was verified

The user asked for (1) a modern look and (2) everything for one PID on
the single `/` dashboard — no navigation to /flame or /kernel needed.
Appraan ran in UI mode (`--seconds 0`) against live LoadApp with
`--kernel-file proof/run5/kernel-fixture.json` (the M3b fixture from
proof/run4, provenance unchanged; a 5 s touch loop emulated the agent
rewriting its --out file, so the feed stayed LIVE: /api/kernel
reported `available:true, source:"file", ageSeconds:1, stale:false,
hint.state:"live"`).

All routes fetched with curl:

| Route | Result |
|---|---|
| `GET /` | 200, 46,217 bytes |
| `GET /flame` | 200, 29,403 bytes |
| `GET /kernel` | 200, 10,827 bytes |
| `GET /api/summary` | 200 — alloc rate 160,760,318 B/s, heapUsed 6,272,000, MaxHeapSize 268,435,456 (the KPI row's data source) |
| `GET /api/gc` | 200 |
| `GET /api/cpu` | 200 |
| `GET /api/cores` | 200 |
| `GET /api/stacks` | 200, 3,062 bytes |
| `GET /api/kernel` | 200 — fixture categories (File 4040 ops, avg 139.0 µs, max 17270.1 µs, kinds, hist) |

Dashboard HTML assertions (28/28 PASS) — the fetched `/` page itself
contains, inline:

- header band with LIVE/STALE badge (`id="live-badge"`), KPI row
  (`kpi-alloc`, `kpi-heap`, `kpi-young`, `kpi-old`, `kpi-cpu`);
- GC card incl. G1 detail (`gc-young`, `g1-split`, …), CPU top-leaf
  table, per-core table;
- thread-stacks card (`id="stacks"`) fed by `fetch('/api/stacks')`;
- **flame graph INLINE**: `<svg>` with **54 `class="frame"` elements**,
  "CPU flame graph — 1706 samples", the hot leaf `LoadApp.isPrime`
  present, Reset-zoom button + Refresh button, and the 15 s
  `fetch('/flame')` in-place refresh;
- kernel card (`kernel-body`, `kernel-cats`, `kernel-threads`,
  `kernel-diag`) with units in words: "Off-CPU (times in milli
  seconds)", "Avg latency (in micro seconds)", "Max latency
  (in micro seconds)";
- the 747698f LIVE/STALE behaviour intact in the page script:
  `setInterval(refresh, 1000)` and
  `staleAfterSec = Math.max(6, cadence * 2.5)`.

Deep-link pages still work: `/kernel` server-renders the fixture
(File/Disk categories, WrQueue wait reason, diagnostics line, units
in words in its headings); `/flame` renders its SVG + frames +
top-leaf table as before.

## Not verified here

- Interactive rendering/click-zoom in a real browser (no browser in
  this VM): the zoom markup + script are the same proven mechanism as
  /flame (proof run 2/4), now class-scoped and rebindable; the
  in-browser click remains for the user's machine, as before.
- No JSON endpoint changed: JsonApi.java is untouched in this change,
  and the payloads above match the pre-upgrade shapes.

## Checks

`./build.sh` (JDK 24) clean; `./run-tests.sh` — **169/169 checks
passed** (KernelCryptoTest 19, KernelDataTest 45, KernelFeedTest 26,
G1StatsTest 26, StacksTest 16, FlameGraphTest 10, JsonTest 20,
KernelIngestTest 7), identical to the pre-upgrade baseline.
